I think we're answering too many questions!

KK Sasa wants the matrix to be parameters, so the
decomposition can't be done in R.

I was also trying to ask if we could make the
Cholesky decomposition more accurate in Stan by
using pivoting.  We need to do more work on
testing positive-definiteness, too, because we
still have the outstanding issue of high-dimensional
correlation and covariance matrix parameters being
rejected for not being positive definite.

- Bob

