On Tuesday, November 26, 2013 12:11:00 AM UTC-5, KK Sasa wrote:
> Thanks for your feedback, Ben. But I indeed need the ordering of elements of eigenvectors and eigenvalues to be fixed as I showed previously in MATLAB, because it will be much more difficult to estimate Sigma matrix without knowing the ordering of elements of Sigma.
> The ordering of elements of Sigma is corresponding to my data matrix.
> Could we modify the eigenvalues_sym and eigenvectors_sym without ordering?

That would require carrying a patch against Eigen, which we are reluctant to do. The order of the eigenvalues and eigenvectors doesn't affect the elements of Sigma. So, you could just change your code so that it assumes the zero eigenvalues come first. Or you could do the eigendecomposition in R beforehand, order things however you want, and pass that to Stan as data.

Ben

