On 11/27/13, 7:11 PM, Ross Boylan wrote:
> extract is quite slow compared to as.array (13 seconds vs 0.3 s).  I was
> a little surprised, and wonder if there's anything that can be done
> about it.

Perhaps --- feel free to look at the source and make a suggestion.

as.array() is a lot simpler.  It returns a flat structure where
only the non-warmup samples are saved as an array.  extract() on
the other hand returns a structured list, as you note below.

Stan's sampler works on the unstructured array, so there's a lot
less work to do to return it.

No idea what's going on with the memory.

- Bob

